      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it. To make the debate really high-level, they should probably touch on the socio-economic arguments too. For example, how did they frame the idea that integrated neighborhoods or schools would lead to \"social chaos\" or economic decline? If they can explain how segregation was framed as a way to protect the stability of the economy and community standards, it'll help them argue that the era's leaders thought they were being \"practical\" rather than just hateful. Can you elaborate on those types of arguments?",
